1
00:00:16,790 --> 00:00:19,860
(Jung Yong Hwa)

2
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:22,160
(Hong Seung Hee)

3
00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:25,960
(Lee Yi Kyung)

4
00:00:27,430 --> 00:00:29,430
(Park Yu Na)

5
00:00:40,710 --> 00:00:43,950
(Oh! My Guard)

6
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:45,550
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

7
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:47,050
(Also, children and animals were filmed under production guidelines.)

8
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:51,190
Don't go anywhere anymore.

9
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:54,590
Just stay by my side.

10
00:01:31,430 --> 00:01:32,560
The phone is turned off.

11
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:34,330
After the beep, you will be connected to voicemail...

12
00:01:40,870 --> 00:01:41,940
Did she just leave?

13
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:45,510
Today, I really...

14
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:48,410
had somewhere I wanted to go together...

15
00:01:55,490 --> 00:01:57,390
Goodness! One, two

16
00:01:57,390 --> 00:02:03,360
I'm in my dream

17
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:06,260
How long do I have to sing this?

18
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:10,440
Am I a walking motion sickness pill?

19
00:02:11,870 --> 00:02:12,870
What else can I do?

20
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:14,910
I only react to your voice.

21
00:02:15,910 --> 00:02:17,980
My body only remembers you.

22
00:02:19,410 --> 00:02:21,410
Please, just one more song, okay? Just one.

23
00:02:26,550 --> 00:02:28,250
If my brother throws up on Ddabong...

24
00:02:41,830 --> 00:02:42,830
Is it that hard for you?

25
00:02:43,670 --> 00:02:44,670
Can you really not handle it?

26
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:48,770
Then we should go somewhere and take a rest.

27
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:54,280
Even over there.

28
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:58,920
(Green Motel)

29
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,350
You...

30
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:03,790
trust me, right?

31
00:03:15,230 --> 00:03:16,830
This is the place you wanted to rest at?

32
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:19,970
Well, what kind of place were you imagining?

33
00:03:22,570 --> 00:03:24,210
I was not imagining anything.

34
00:03:25,140 --> 00:03:27,750
Although, I do have a pretty wild imagination.

35
00:03:27,910 --> 00:03:29,210
Since I am always stuck at home,

36
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:31,420
I imagined everything that happens outside.

37
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:34,320
That is why that man always called me Anne of Green Gables...

38
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:42,460
That man? What man? Do you mean Director Han Jung Woo?

39
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:46,360
No, not Director Han.

40
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:50,540
Come to think of it, who was that man?

41
00:03:55,070 --> 00:03:57,880
Wait. You said you were stuck at home.

42
00:03:58,280 --> 00:04:02,410
- So your... - Me? What do you mean?

43
00:04:02,810 --> 00:04:05,680
What? I love wandering around outside as a hobby.

44
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:10,020
Anyway, I finally feel alive.

45
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:14,860
By the way,

46
00:04:15,430 --> 00:04:17,230
there is no one at the playground.

47
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:20,830
It was raining until just a moment ago.

48
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:23,400
It is nice that no one recognises me.

49
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:27,810
But I achieved my dream, so...

50
00:04:29,110 --> 00:04:30,710
I have to endure that kind of inconvenience.

51
00:04:33,580 --> 00:04:34,610
By the way,

52
00:04:35,550 --> 00:04:37,080
was being an actor always your dream?

53
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:39,520
Not a car designer?

54
00:04:40,490 --> 00:04:41,990
That is just a story in a drama.

55
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:44,060
Do you think the me you know is the real me?

56
00:04:46,490 --> 00:04:48,390
Rich people must have multiple dreams.

57
00:04:49,130 --> 00:04:51,930
I suppose you can achieve them more easily than others.

58
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:54,670
You really do not know anything.

59
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:56,970
I crawled my way up from the very bottom.

60
00:04:57,100 --> 00:05:00,040
Things used to never work out for me.

61
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:02,810
I am rookie actor Kim Jae Hee. Thank you.

62
00:05:02,870 --> 00:05:03,980
I look forward to working with you.

63
00:05:06,580 --> 00:05:08,150
Back when I did not even have a chance,

64
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:10,310
giving up was easy.

65
00:05:11,250 --> 00:05:12,920
Let us stop, man.

66
00:05:13,220 --> 00:05:14,720
But it turns out...

67
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:17,760
there are many people like me in the world.

68
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:20,360
I gave up on my dream today.

69
00:05:20,930 --> 00:05:24,360
Right now, I am the most depressed person in the world.

70
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:34,110
I am more depressed than you.

71
00:05:34,370 --> 00:05:36,310
- I do not have a single friend. - I do not have a single friend.

72
00:05:36,670 --> 00:05:38,210
Your ID is Ghost?

73
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:41,080
Just because of that?

74
00:05:42,910 --> 00:05:45,950
I've only had 3 minor roles in 4 years.

75
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:49,650
I'm just a total loser.

76
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:51,390
(I'm just a total loser)

77
00:05:54,990 --> 00:05:58,400
I haven't stepped outside my house in over 15 years.

78
00:05:58,730 --> 00:06:00,100
What a load of crap.

79
00:06:02,830 --> 00:06:04,740
You're such a liar.

80
00:06:06,370 --> 00:06:07,610
It's true.

81
00:06:08,870 --> 00:06:09,870
I swear.

82
00:06:11,310 --> 00:06:13,210
Are you trying to have a battle...

83
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:14,610
over who has the more depressing life?

84
00:06:17,450 --> 00:06:19,420
There are three of us guys...

85
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:23,120
splitting the rent for a rooftop room.

86
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:28,660
I haven't even been to school since the second grade.

87
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:30,630
Today, my profile went straight into the trash...

88
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:33,400
right in front of me.

89
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:38,800
But you probably still have someone who likes you, right?

90
00:06:43,340 --> 00:06:47,450
- I don't even have a mom. - Hey, why are you...

91
00:06:48,810 --> 00:06:50,480
getting so deep all of a sudden?

92
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:53,750
No one likes me.

93
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:56,190
Not even my dad.

94
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:58,020
That's why...

95
00:07:02,660 --> 00:07:05,300
I never smile.

96
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:06,860
What's with her?

97
00:07:07,870 --> 00:07:11,100
How is her life a bigger sob story than mine?

98
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:13,470
She's an attention seeker. A total attention seeker.

99
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:22,480
Yes, yes, you win the award for the most depressing life.

100
00:07:22,550 --> 00:07:24,750
(Ghost: Yes, yes, you win the award for the most depressing life.)

101
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:29,220
(User: Ghost)

102
00:07:32,190 --> 00:07:33,220
Could it be...

103
00:07:34,890 --> 00:07:35,990
true?

104
00:07:43,130 --> 00:07:44,970
Someone I know once said this.

105
00:07:45,770 --> 00:07:49,110
Life is like a box of chocolates.

106
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:52,740
You never know which chocolate you're going to eat first.

107
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:54,150
But one thing is for sure.

108
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:56,880
There are definitely sweet chocolates...

109
00:07:56,950 --> 00:07:59,320
in your box too, Ghost.

110
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:02,590
And maybe in mine as well.

111
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:09,490
If you know that,

112
00:08:10,260 --> 00:08:11,900
why did you say you were giving up earlier?

113
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:15,670
Who even said that?

114
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:27,310
You're stuck at home,

115
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:28,680
so why aren't you answering your phone?

116
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:31,050
Why are you yelling at me?

117
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:33,450
What, are we having a yelling battle now?

118
00:08:33,620 --> 00:08:34,620
What is he talking about?

119
00:08:36,290 --> 00:08:37,290
I told you to eat proper meals,

120
00:08:37,390 --> 00:08:38,790
but you're sitting there eating raw ramyeon.

121
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:40,590
Seriously...

122
00:08:41,230 --> 00:08:42,730
Why is he yelling at me?

123
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:49,130
After that, I visited that cafe a few times,

124
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:52,540
but she never showed up.

125
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:54,340
Do you want to meet her again?

126
00:08:55,210 --> 00:08:56,210
I just...

127
00:08:57,910 --> 00:08:58,980
think about her sometimes.

128
00:09:00,340 --> 00:09:01,350
That Ghost.

129
00:09:02,450 --> 00:09:04,880
I wonder if she knows I became an actor.

130
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,120
That day...

131
00:09:08,290 --> 00:09:10,320
I wonder if she even heard what I said that day.

132
00:09:11,390 --> 00:09:12,420
Hello.

133
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:15,160
You received the Brave Citizen Award for this incident.

134
00:09:15,430 --> 00:09:17,960
Please look at the camera and say a few words.

135
00:09:18,660 --> 00:09:20,160
Aspiring actor Kim...

136
00:09:22,370 --> 00:09:24,540
I mean, Um Tae Bong. I will do my best.

137
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:27,740
May I say one more thing?

138
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:31,480
- I really need to be on television. - Yes, please keep it short.

139
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:33,440
Are you watching?

140
00:09:34,210 --> 00:09:36,180
Ghost, you are watching, right?

141
00:09:36,780 --> 00:09:37,880
I am on television.

142
00:09:38,350 --> 00:09:41,320
Therefore, my chocolate is incredibly sweet.

143
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:42,820
How about you?

144
00:09:43,320 --> 00:09:46,820
Are you still in that serious mode where you never smile?

145
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:50,530
Soon, you will also be able to eat sweets that knock you out, like me.

146
00:09:51,030 --> 00:09:53,560
So smile from now on.

147
00:09:55,100 --> 00:09:58,100
Maybe she already knows.

148
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:02,540
Well, I am not that Ghost,

149
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:06,080
but she definitely heard you.

150
00:10:07,310 --> 00:10:08,350
And...

151
00:10:09,310 --> 00:10:10,350
she probably smiled.

152
00:10:11,220 --> 00:10:13,650
When there is no one to see you smile.

153
00:10:15,250 --> 00:10:16,990
No one smiles alone.

154
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,960
When there is no one to smile with you.

155
00:10:20,390 --> 00:10:23,390
And you feel terribly lonely.

156
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:26,700
Maybe at that moment...

157
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:30,070
you were on her side.

158
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:33,770
Think of it as me always watching over you.

159
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:37,140
So now, you have to smile even if you are alone.

160
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:38,540
(Um Tae Bong, 26 Brave Citizen Award)

161
00:10:39,510 --> 00:10:40,540
Knowing that somewhere...

162
00:10:41,810 --> 00:10:42,980
there is someone on my side.

163
00:10:45,150 --> 00:10:47,620
That alone is enough to make you smile again.

164
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:52,490
You asked who said that back then, right?

165
00:10:53,460 --> 00:10:54,660
Forrest Gump.

166
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:56,560
His mother.

167
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,870
What you gave Ghost that day...

168
00:11:03,430 --> 00:11:04,500
was true comfort.

169
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:07,570
I just...

170
00:11:09,010 --> 00:11:11,040
said what I wanted to hear myself.

171
00:11:11,810 --> 00:11:13,380
Then Ghost, who was right there at that moment,

172
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:15,010
was also comforting you.

173
00:11:16,010 --> 00:11:18,380
She made your life, which almost went down the wrong path that day,

174
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:21,290
take a U-turn. Since you know that,

175
00:11:22,350 --> 00:11:23,820
why did you say you were giving up earlier?

176
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:33,360
You have to do the same for me.

177
00:11:34,330 --> 00:11:36,530
If I am going down the wrong path.

178
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:38,470
But I keep going without realising it.

179
00:11:38,540 --> 00:11:42,970
Then you have to appear right in front of me,

180
00:11:48,180 --> 00:11:50,250
so I can return to where I belong.

181
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:53,780
I want you to do that for me too.

182
00:11:55,990 --> 00:11:56,990
You will do that, right?

183
00:12:01,190 --> 00:12:04,130
Nothing in this world is free. Then give me money. Money.

184
00:12:04,530 --> 00:12:05,730
I do not have any.

185
00:12:06,130 --> 00:12:09,130
You are just going to exchange it for coins anyway.

186
00:12:09,930 --> 00:12:11,640
If you do not give it to me today,

187
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:14,770
- I will bulldoze this place. - Do whatever you want.

188
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:17,410
There is not a single customer today...

189
00:12:17,810 --> 00:12:19,310
Wait, there is one.

190
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:22,780
Seriously, give me the money. Money.

191
00:12:22,850 --> 00:12:25,850
Sir, give me money.

192
00:12:26,380 --> 00:12:28,320
Money.

193
00:12:29,450 --> 00:12:30,590
What are you doing right now?

194
00:12:34,760 --> 00:12:36,430
That crazy guy from last time?

195
00:12:36,790 --> 00:12:38,500
That crazy woman from last time?

196
00:12:39,460 --> 00:12:40,530
What, crazy?

197
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:44,030
- Are you talking to me right now? - Are you extorting money here too?

198
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:46,140
What for this time?

199
00:12:49,370 --> 00:12:50,710
To be on television over there?

200
00:12:51,380 --> 00:12:53,180
No, but why are you extorting money here?

201
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:56,250
Extorting? She is our lord.

202
00:12:56,880 --> 00:12:57,880
Lord?

203
00:12:58,580 --> 00:13:00,480
Our landlord.

204
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:04,050
Ready, go.

205
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:08,660
But are you really the landlord?

206
00:13:10,030 --> 00:13:11,200
None of your business.

207
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:13,330
You have a very unique taste in investments.

208
00:13:14,330 --> 00:13:16,330
They said the value would double in just one year.

209
00:13:17,330 --> 00:13:20,200
But after selling this to me, the real estate agent ran away.

210
00:13:21,170 --> 00:13:23,310
Gosh, dead again.

211
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:26,810
But no one knows there is an arcade in the alley,

212
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:27,880
and no one comes here.

213
00:13:28,350 --> 00:13:29,910
Seven, six,

214
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:34,350
- five, four, three... - Behind you.

215
00:13:44,130 --> 00:13:45,900
(Tekken King Han Jung Woo Was Here. Oct 7, 2001)

216
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:48,330
Han Jung Woo was here for the last time?

217
00:13:50,170 --> 00:13:51,870
I wrote that the day before I immigrated to the UK.

218
00:13:51,970 --> 00:13:53,870
Two thousand one?

219
00:13:55,570 --> 00:13:56,570
Then for 20 years,

220
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:58,140
this place has not been painted once?

221
00:13:58,480 --> 00:14:02,110
I wondered who would buy a building as old as me,

222
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:04,250
and this young celebrity bought it.

223
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:08,520
My life as a landlord is completely ruined.

224
00:14:08,620 --> 00:14:11,220
Just stop here for today and go home.

225
00:14:11,290 --> 00:14:13,960
You only take a quarter of the rent,

226
00:14:14,260 --> 00:14:18,130
and on months with no customers, you change even that into coins...

227
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:23,470
and spend it all here. To help me pay the electric bill.

228
00:14:24,270 --> 00:14:25,270
Wait a minute.

229
00:14:26,670 --> 00:14:29,440
- Just one more game. - What, one game?

230
00:14:50,330 --> 00:14:51,330
Father.

231
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:53,800
I am home.

232
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:08,880
What is it? It is not like you came out to see me off,

233
00:15:09,380 --> 00:15:10,910
so you must have something to say. What is it?

234
00:15:12,020 --> 00:15:13,480
Cha Hong Du's real family,

235
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:16,150
how is it...

236
00:15:17,050 --> 00:15:18,120
that no one is looking for her?

237
00:15:19,220 --> 00:15:20,360
They are not looking because no one exists.

238
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:21,460
I looked into it, too.

239
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:24,500
They say her mother passed away a long time ago,

240
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:26,860
and it seems she has a father.

241
00:15:27,460 --> 00:15:28,470
To the young lady...

242
00:15:29,870 --> 00:15:33,170
- it is as if he does not exist. - I have a bad feeling about it...

243
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:36,040
A normal father would have already been looking for her.

244
00:15:36,110 --> 00:15:37,240
And filed a missing person report.

245
00:15:37,610 --> 00:15:38,710
What is Cha Hong Du's real name?

246
00:15:38,710 --> 00:15:40,180
You will get hurt if you know that.

247
00:15:41,510 --> 00:15:42,680
Why is that important?

248
00:15:42,750 --> 00:15:44,280
You are not even going to call her by that name.

249
00:15:47,950 --> 00:15:49,050
What now?

250
00:15:52,790 --> 00:15:53,790
Why are you coming closer?

251
00:15:54,090 --> 00:15:55,090
From the beginning...

252
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,800
there was no blackmail, was there?

253
00:16:04,740 --> 00:16:07,300
Fine, fine, let us say...

254
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:10,670
I lied to you. Are you happy now?

255
00:16:10,810 --> 00:16:12,240
Are you a secret donation angel or something?

256
00:16:12,310 --> 00:16:14,580
Let us say I also knew about Hong Du's pitiful situation...

257
00:16:14,650 --> 00:16:16,510
and did it because I wanted to help her.

258
00:16:18,020 --> 00:16:21,420
Okay, okay, I will look for a place for Hong Du to go right now, okay?

259
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:23,250
You cold-hearted jerk.

260
00:16:24,090 --> 00:16:25,090
Take your time.

261
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:28,160
There is no rush.

262
00:16:33,460 --> 00:16:35,570
Does he think he is Richard Gere? Darn it.

263
00:16:36,970 --> 00:16:38,270
He is such a show-off, this punk.

264
00:16:41,210 --> 00:16:42,210
Hey.

265
00:16:44,780 --> 00:16:47,850
- You should get here earlier. - Su Dong worked hard today too,

266
00:16:48,110 --> 00:16:49,450
so let us drink until we drop.

267
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:56,990
Yang Soo Dong, what is it? Why are you in such a good mood?

268
00:16:59,390 --> 00:17:01,490
Where did Yang Soo Dong go...

269
00:17:01,630 --> 00:17:03,290
after running away from the broadcasting station today?

270
00:17:08,100 --> 00:17:10,230
Well, while he was away,

271
00:17:10,300 --> 00:17:12,640
I thought I would clean his house for him.

272
00:17:12,870 --> 00:17:15,340
- You know? Like a secret helper. - You did?

273
00:17:15,410 --> 00:17:16,610
Why has our Ghost not been contacting us...

274
00:17:16,710 --> 00:17:19,380
to buy anything lately?

275
00:17:20,180 --> 00:17:21,280
Did they stop being a fan?

276
00:17:25,520 --> 00:17:27,120
- Mr. Choi Gu? - You thief.

277
00:17:27,180 --> 00:17:28,620
There was a rumour that That Person has dementia.

278
00:17:28,690 --> 00:17:30,220
So he was staying at Tae Bong's house.

279
00:17:30,290 --> 00:17:33,290
And I found a very important...

280
00:17:33,360 --> 00:17:36,330
- piece of evidence there. - Evidence?

281
00:17:36,390 --> 00:17:38,360
Undeniable evidence that Cha Hong Du...

282
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:40,330
has been going in and out of that house.

283
00:17:40,830 --> 00:17:43,400
I mean, ever since she showed up,

284
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:45,540
he told us not to come anywhere near his house.

285
00:17:45,770 --> 00:17:49,410
He even goes to the set on his own. She is young, but...

286
00:17:49,470 --> 00:17:54,140
she talks down to him all the time. And he only stares at her on set.

287
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:57,650
Putting all of that together,

288
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:01,690
- the two of them are dating. - No way.

289
00:18:02,190 --> 00:18:06,090
And that is Um Tae Bong's fatal flaw.

290
00:18:06,490 --> 00:18:09,790
- What are you talking about? - He has terrible taste in women.

291
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:12,630
Hey, does she have money or a good education?

292
00:18:13,100 --> 00:18:14,100
And that girl has the nerve...

293
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:16,170
to show up acting like a secret bodyguard.

294
00:18:18,670 --> 00:18:21,670
Hong Du was a secret bodyguard?

295
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:23,440
That is crazy.

296
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:26,840
So what I mean is...

297
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:30,350
Anyway, that is not what is important.

298
00:18:30,510 --> 00:18:33,380
Um Tae Bong has been deceiving Toxic Na Ri all this time...

299
00:18:33,450 --> 00:18:34,450
What?

300
00:18:35,620 --> 00:18:36,850
Who is deceiving our Na Ri?

301
00:18:55,540 --> 00:18:57,170
Why does it have to be my drama?

302
00:19:02,050 --> 00:19:03,350
Look at you.

303
00:19:04,010 --> 00:19:05,550
I knew you would be like this.

304
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:07,020
Like what?

305
00:19:07,450 --> 00:19:09,690
Fine, I will be generous.

306
00:19:14,220 --> 00:19:15,230
Here.

307
00:19:15,960 --> 00:19:17,760
(Cha Hong Du One-Day Pass)

308
00:19:17,900 --> 00:19:20,830
You were holding out here just to get a birthday present.

309
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:22,200
I definitely gave you one.

310
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:24,670
So I will expect one on my birthday too.

311
00:19:29,140 --> 00:19:31,940
Wow, does she think she is an amusement park?

312
00:19:33,910 --> 00:19:37,880
One, two, three, four...

313
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:41,250
Why did she draw one more than the stars?

314
00:19:45,460 --> 00:19:48,330
(Jubong Sweet and Spicy Fried Chicken)

315
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:54,600
The neighbourhood where Hae Ra was caught on CCTV,

316
00:19:54,670 --> 00:19:56,070
I would like to go there myself.

317
00:19:56,600 --> 00:19:57,870
I have not seen her at all since then,

318
00:19:57,940 --> 00:19:59,900
so I do not think she is from this neighbourhood.

319
00:20:02,670 --> 00:20:03,740
Let us go check over there too.

320
00:20:04,340 --> 00:20:05,340
Yes, sir.

321
00:20:09,410 --> 00:20:11,850
We should head back now. The sun has already set.

322
00:20:16,090 --> 00:20:17,090
Chairman Oh.

323
00:20:20,290 --> 00:20:21,290
Yes.

324
00:20:21,530 --> 00:20:22,860
What brings you to my neighbourhood?

325
00:20:23,190 --> 00:20:24,830
Was this where you lived, Director Han?

326
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:26,260
Yes.

327
00:20:26,930 --> 00:20:29,230
I live in that penthouse over there.

328
00:20:33,070 --> 00:20:34,070
Han Jung Woo,

329
00:20:35,310 --> 00:20:37,110
why this rooftop apartment of all places?

330
00:20:42,350 --> 00:20:43,350
Director Han,

331
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:45,780
are you adjusting well now that you are back in Korea?

332
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:47,520
Yes, I am trying my best.

333
00:20:48,950 --> 00:20:51,250
Right, whose side are you on, Director Han?

334
00:20:52,420 --> 00:20:54,790
- Excuse me? - There is no need to play innocent.

335
00:20:54,860 --> 00:20:56,490
You must have figured it out by now.

336
00:20:56,560 --> 00:20:58,500
Whether it is Chairman Oh or Chairman Wang.

337
00:20:58,800 --> 00:21:00,000
It is time to pick a side.

338
00:21:00,360 --> 00:21:01,900
Well, I...

339
00:21:01,970 --> 00:21:03,370
Actually, for this new car promotion,

340
00:21:03,430 --> 00:21:05,340
your insight played a big role,

341
00:21:05,440 --> 00:21:07,400
and thanks to that, sales have exceeded expectations.

342
00:21:07,970 --> 00:21:10,040
Whichever side you choose, Director Han...

343
00:21:10,540 --> 00:21:13,840
is now a force the company cannot ignore, right?

344
00:21:15,380 --> 00:21:16,450
There is no need to rush.

345
00:21:16,950 --> 00:21:18,550
Once the heiress reveals herself to the world,

346
00:21:18,620 --> 00:21:20,580
the direction of the wind will change.

347
00:21:20,780 --> 00:21:24,190
- We should join forces then. - Of course we should.

348
00:21:24,590 --> 00:21:26,590
Eat, eat up.

349
00:21:27,220 --> 00:21:28,230
Why...

350
00:21:29,530 --> 00:21:30,930
I should be doing that.

351
00:21:33,230 --> 00:21:34,400
It is hot.

352
00:21:35,930 --> 00:21:38,170
Did you enjoy your meal with the directors?

353
00:21:38,270 --> 00:21:39,970
Next time, please make sure to include me...

354
00:21:40,470 --> 00:21:42,110
- Yes, I will. - Yes, yes.

355
00:21:42,170 --> 00:21:43,170
- Manager Na. - Yes.

356
00:21:44,510 --> 00:21:46,280
About our company's heiress.

357
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:48,580
Do you know anything about her?

358
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:55,490
As the best informant in the company,

359
00:21:56,390 --> 00:21:58,160
this is a top secret...

360
00:21:59,890 --> 00:22:01,860
I heard she is incredibly ugly...

361
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:03,530
What?

362
00:22:03,590 --> 00:22:07,200
This is a secret even the directors do not know, yes.

363
00:22:09,330 --> 00:22:12,300
That man is Reporter No Tae Hwan.

364
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:14,600
He used to write a lot of articles about our company.

365
00:22:15,870 --> 00:22:16,870
Where is he going?

366
00:22:18,580 --> 00:22:19,640
No Tae Hwan?

367
00:22:21,780 --> 00:22:24,680
(A "Car Doll Keychain" That Did Not Fit the Scene Was Found...)

368
00:22:24,750 --> 00:22:26,050
(Reporter No Tae Hwan)

369
00:22:29,050 --> 00:22:30,750
- Manager Na, go inside first. - Yes.

370
00:22:31,090 --> 00:22:32,160
Excuse me?

371
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:35,260
Excuse me, sir.

372
00:22:35,930 --> 00:22:37,530
You are Reporter No Tae Hwan, right?

373
00:22:38,060 --> 00:22:40,200
I work at BK, and my name is Han Jung Woo.

374
00:22:40,660 --> 00:22:42,630
I read the article you wrote before.

375
00:22:43,370 --> 00:22:45,000
About Wang Hui Yeon.

376
00:22:46,670 --> 00:22:49,840
Why did you view that accident as a mystery?

377
00:22:51,810 --> 00:22:54,180
It is refreshing to hear such a question...

378
00:22:54,240 --> 00:22:55,250
from someone at BK.

379
00:22:58,550 --> 00:22:59,550
She turned it.

380
00:23:00,550 --> 00:23:01,550
Excuse me?

381
00:23:02,720 --> 00:23:05,160
That woman turned the steering wheel herself.

382
00:23:07,090 --> 00:23:09,190
What do you...

383
00:23:09,760 --> 00:23:13,100
It was a fatal accident where she crashed into a parked truck,

384
00:23:13,300 --> 00:23:14,530
and someone went to the inquiring reporter...

385
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:16,670
and gave him money.

386
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:18,270
Enough money that he would not have to...

387
00:23:18,340 --> 00:23:19,340
work as a reporter anymore.

388
00:23:21,470 --> 00:23:24,070
Excuse me, sir. Just one more thing.

389
00:23:24,140 --> 00:23:25,340
The car doll keychain...

390
00:23:25,440 --> 00:23:27,110
that was found there at the time, right?

391
00:23:27,180 --> 00:23:28,210
What did you hear?

392
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:30,480
I told you I received the money.

393
00:23:31,410 --> 00:23:33,450
I am the kind of person who earns his keep.

394
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:55,040
Mom!

395
00:23:59,280 --> 00:24:00,280
Cha Hong Du.

396
00:24:02,750 --> 00:24:03,750
Cha Hong Du.

397
00:24:35,680 --> 00:24:38,720
(We Have Noodles)

398
00:24:42,190 --> 00:24:44,350
Why are you not answering? Are you mad?

399
00:24:45,590 --> 00:24:47,220
(Song Na Ri, Actor and Singer, Country Girls)

400
00:24:50,260 --> 00:24:52,860
He was so touched by the arm sleeves I gave him.

401
00:24:53,430 --> 00:24:55,270
We look pretty good together.

402
00:24:57,500 --> 00:24:58,600
I think I should get going.

403
00:24:59,300 --> 00:25:00,300
We can talk later.

404
00:25:03,640 --> 00:25:05,680
Did he really go to her yesterday?

405
00:25:08,680 --> 00:25:10,150
I thought it was a contract relationship.

406
00:25:17,820 --> 00:25:20,020
The number you have reached is not available.

407
00:25:20,120 --> 00:25:21,660
After the beep, you will be connected to voicemail...

408
00:25:24,130 --> 00:25:27,330
(Are you mad? I just need some air...)

409
00:25:27,500 --> 00:25:30,400
- Who did you piss off this time? - Gosh, you startled me.

410
00:25:31,330 --> 00:25:33,940
The bad boy concept is only cool in dramas.

411
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:35,170
In reality, it is a total failure.

412
00:25:35,370 --> 00:25:37,140
You really cannot tell the difference...

413
00:25:37,210 --> 00:25:38,410
between dramas and reality.

414
00:25:39,040 --> 00:25:41,910
Wow, look who is talking.

415
00:25:42,510 --> 00:25:45,780
But why does your face look like that after a nap?

416
00:25:46,080 --> 00:25:49,190
I had a freaking amazing dream. Should I buy a lottery ticket?

417
00:25:50,250 --> 00:25:51,250
What dream?

418
00:25:53,490 --> 00:25:54,520
A dream where you died.

419
00:25:54,860 --> 00:25:57,130
- What? - You got shot to death.

420
00:25:57,760 --> 00:26:01,300
What a shame. I should have shot you.

421
00:26:01,930 --> 00:26:02,930
Bang.

422
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:05,200
That little...

423
00:26:07,100 --> 00:26:09,170
A dream where I get shot to death?

424
00:26:19,080 --> 00:26:22,990
Why are all my dreams just one nightmare after another?

425
00:26:25,520 --> 00:26:27,690
Anyway, they both leave a bad taste in my mouth.

426
00:26:35,330 --> 00:26:38,230
(The Crown Prince's Bodyguard)

427
00:26:42,970 --> 00:26:44,540
Han Jung Woo.

428
00:26:55,290 --> 00:26:57,320
This was the last scene.

429
00:27:03,930 --> 00:27:05,960
That is what I am saying.

430
00:27:07,030 --> 00:27:08,030
I know.

431
00:27:08,100 --> 00:27:10,670
I know very well that you are Toxic Na Ri's manager.

432
00:27:10,730 --> 00:27:13,140
But if Toxic Na Ri finds out about this,

433
00:27:13,200 --> 00:27:15,270
she is going to completely lose her mind.

434
00:27:15,340 --> 00:27:17,110
(Blank Check)

435
00:27:20,940 --> 00:27:21,950
Yes.

436
00:27:22,010 --> 00:27:24,410
- No advances on your salary. - That is not it.

437
00:27:29,190 --> 00:27:30,220
I am so sorry.

438
00:27:30,550 --> 00:27:32,820
- For what? - About Tae Bong and Hong Du dating,

439
00:27:32,890 --> 00:27:35,560
I swear I did not intentionally snitch...

440
00:27:35,630 --> 00:27:37,990
- to Song Na Ri's manager. - Wait, hold on.

441
00:27:38,060 --> 00:27:40,960
- Who is dating who? - Tae Bong and Cha Hong Du.

442
00:27:41,730 --> 00:27:44,370
It is an open secret among all of us...

443
00:27:44,370 --> 00:27:45,500
No, it is not.

444
00:27:46,200 --> 00:27:48,970
CEO Park, do not worry. I will find a way...

445
00:27:49,040 --> 00:27:53,340
- to tear them apart somehow. - No, do not do that. Do not.

446
00:27:53,980 --> 00:27:55,080
Mom.

447
00:27:55,650 --> 00:27:57,510
You know the implant money you mentioned before.

448
00:27:57,850 --> 00:27:58,950
Yes, I have it ready.

449
00:28:01,520 --> 00:28:03,190
The CEO gave it to me?

450
00:28:05,290 --> 00:28:07,220
I wonder why he gave it to me.

451
00:28:07,920 --> 00:28:08,930
What?

452
00:28:10,060 --> 00:28:11,460
Eyelid surgery?

453
00:28:13,500 --> 00:28:15,270
How much is that going to cost?

454
00:28:16,230 --> 00:28:17,700
(Blank Check)

455
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:19,400
Let us just keep this one thing, just this.

456
00:28:22,510 --> 00:28:23,570
(Do not live like that.)

457
00:28:24,370 --> 00:28:26,210
(We will meet, right?)

458
00:28:26,280 --> 00:28:27,840
I think we need to find out...

459
00:28:27,910 --> 00:28:29,010
if all of these were sent by one person.

460
00:28:29,210 --> 00:28:30,280
Right.

461
00:28:32,320 --> 00:28:33,950
Yes, thank you. I will call you later.

462
00:28:35,750 --> 00:28:37,190
It is your day off, so where are you going?

463
00:28:39,290 --> 00:28:40,520
I have nothing to wear.

464
00:28:41,020 --> 00:28:43,660
I am going out to buy some clothes and get some fresh air.

465
00:28:43,960 --> 00:28:44,960
I will be back.

466
00:28:46,030 --> 00:28:47,430
Then will you not go see my brother...

467
00:28:55,210 --> 00:28:56,710
I can finally breathe.

468
00:28:59,810 --> 00:29:01,040
Are you feeling a bit better?

469
00:29:01,380 --> 00:29:03,280
Because I left you like that yesterday,

470
00:29:03,380 --> 00:29:05,980
you were a little angry. Our Hyun Joo.

471
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:09,190
Keep looking at me like you are posing for a photoshoot.

472
00:29:10,120 --> 00:29:12,660
Then I might just feel like forgiving you.

473
00:29:14,990 --> 00:29:17,090
The standard for a photoshoot pose...

474
00:29:17,690 --> 00:29:18,700
is this.

475
00:29:22,570 --> 00:29:23,570
You smiled.

476
00:29:26,940 --> 00:29:28,100
You abandoned me...

477
00:29:28,170 --> 00:29:29,910
and had a good time with your girlfriend?

478
00:29:30,810 --> 00:29:32,240
I saw Song Na Ri's Instagram.

479
00:29:34,910 --> 00:29:35,910
That?

480
00:29:36,150 --> 00:29:37,780
This is why only those without someone feel sad.

481
00:29:38,580 --> 00:29:41,620
I am starting to get jealous. It makes me want to steal you away.

482
00:29:42,090 --> 00:29:43,720
That is the best thing I have heard all day.

483
00:29:43,950 --> 00:29:46,620
If I steal you? Will you fall for me?

484
00:29:48,120 --> 00:29:49,290
I just might.

485
00:29:51,330 --> 00:29:53,000
Then should we start with a kiss?

486
00:29:53,830 --> 00:29:55,000
That is the natural order.

487
00:29:56,530 --> 00:29:58,270
- Suddenly? - Yes.

488
00:29:58,900 --> 00:30:00,100
I said let us try it.

489
00:30:03,710 --> 00:30:06,210
You never used to give me an inch,

490
00:30:06,480 --> 00:30:07,980
but now you are just throwing yourself at me?

491
00:30:08,910 --> 00:30:10,310
Why? Do you hate it?

492
00:30:13,020 --> 00:30:14,020
What?

493
00:30:21,360 --> 00:30:22,990
There will be no kissing between us.

494
00:30:23,730 --> 00:30:24,860
That is...

495
00:30:25,090 --> 00:30:26,660
because out of all the ways I express my affection...

496
00:30:26,730 --> 00:30:27,860
for you, Hyun Joo,

497
00:30:28,930 --> 00:30:30,500
it is the most trivial.

498
00:30:45,550 --> 00:30:47,050
My father is going to get even prettier.

499
00:30:50,190 --> 00:30:53,260
Father. What was I like when I was young?

500
00:30:54,060 --> 00:30:55,490
No matter how hard I try to remember,

501
00:30:55,630 --> 00:30:56,890
I cannot remember.

502
00:30:57,490 --> 00:30:58,700
Mister.

503
00:30:59,230 --> 00:31:01,100
Why do you keep staring at me?

504
00:31:02,430 --> 00:31:03,500
I do not like it.

505
00:31:03,570 --> 00:31:05,700
Is this the time to worry about my lost memories?

506
00:31:05,770 --> 00:31:07,700
Father is always fighting with himself.

507
00:31:10,140 --> 00:31:11,140
But Father,

508
00:31:12,180 --> 00:31:15,610
to be honest, I am scared to protect Um Tae Bong.

509
00:31:17,010 --> 00:31:19,720
I only caught that pickpocket by chance last time.

510
00:31:19,980 --> 00:31:22,390
Even in front of that fan who was bothering Song Na Ri,

511
00:31:22,450 --> 00:31:23,720
I was actually terrified.

512
00:31:24,790 --> 00:31:28,090
I was always brave and courageous,

513
00:31:28,560 --> 00:31:29,890
but strangely,

514
00:31:30,530 --> 00:31:32,260
it feels like that was not me at all.

515
00:31:32,560 --> 00:31:33,760
If...

516
00:31:33,830 --> 00:31:36,230
something actually happens to Um Tae Bong...

517
00:31:38,430 --> 00:31:40,240
I am afraid I will not be able to do anything.

518
00:31:41,400 --> 00:31:43,340
That is what scares me the most, Father.

519
00:31:44,910 --> 00:31:45,910
Hey.

520
00:31:46,110 --> 00:31:48,950
- What are you doing to his hair? - You are here?

521
00:31:49,380 --> 00:31:51,580
I have always been the one to cut my father's hair, why?

522
00:31:51,650 --> 00:31:52,820
It looks perfectly fine.

523
00:31:52,880 --> 00:31:57,390
- Right, Father? - Chop, chop, what a flop!

524
00:31:57,450 --> 00:32:00,120
My hair is uneven!

525
00:32:02,130 --> 00:32:03,130
In that case,

526
00:32:03,190 --> 00:32:04,690
let's cut this part again. Just here.

527
00:32:09,600 --> 00:32:11,730
I might go to the rooftop room this weekend.

528
00:32:12,100 --> 00:32:13,440
Do whatever you want.

529
00:32:13,770 --> 00:32:16,110
Well, I have some clothes to bring back.

530
00:32:16,810 --> 00:32:18,410
You do not even have any clothes to bring.

531
00:32:18,780 --> 00:32:20,610
Well, I will not go if you do not want me to.

532
00:32:21,310 --> 00:32:22,310
Are you kidding me?

533
00:32:22,380 --> 00:32:23,950
"At 3:30 on Wednesday afternoon,"

534
00:32:24,010 --> 00:32:25,010
"Han,"

535
00:32:25,080 --> 00:32:27,350
"do you want to go ride bikes again this weekend?"

536
00:32:28,380 --> 00:32:29,720
Who sent that?

537
00:32:30,720 --> 00:32:32,190
I never said that.

538
00:32:34,120 --> 00:32:36,690
Just go. Did anyone stop you?

539
00:32:37,330 --> 00:32:39,430
Bring me some water first. He is thirsty.

540
00:32:50,470 --> 00:32:53,710
Should I try an undercut while we are at it?

541
00:32:54,710 --> 00:32:55,710
What do you think, Tae Bong?

542
00:33:00,650 --> 00:33:02,590
Sir?

543
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:09,860
While I was out of my mind,

544
00:33:09,930 --> 00:33:11,990
I gained another daughter I never had.

545
00:33:13,860 --> 00:33:14,860
I am sorry.

546
00:33:15,330 --> 00:33:18,170
For bringing you here without asking.

547
00:33:18,230 --> 00:33:19,570
No, it is fine.

548
00:33:20,500 --> 00:33:22,570
I used to make a living off my face,

549
00:33:22,640 --> 00:33:25,710
so thank you for keeping me from looking terrible in public.

550
00:33:29,650 --> 00:33:30,710
From now on...

551
00:33:32,680 --> 00:33:34,920
things will only get worse, right?

552
00:33:38,650 --> 00:33:42,160
If I forget this conversation too...

553
00:33:44,530 --> 00:33:45,700
what do I do then?

554
00:33:48,200 --> 00:33:49,430
I have done...

555
00:33:49,970 --> 00:33:51,530
a great wrong to you, sir.

556
00:33:51,670 --> 00:33:53,640
- I will stop. - Do not.

557
00:33:56,110 --> 00:33:59,610
Look at her smiling so innocently. Just a few more days.

558
00:34:00,310 --> 00:34:01,340
That much...

559
00:34:02,610 --> 00:34:04,350
My daughter will understand.

560
00:34:07,620 --> 00:34:10,420
("Red Snowman")

561
00:34:37,150 --> 00:34:38,450
(Filming The Cocky Detective and Con Artist)

562
00:34:38,510 --> 00:34:42,120
Cha Hong Du. You look pretty today.

563
00:34:43,650 --> 00:34:45,560
Did you change your makeup?

564
00:34:45,990 --> 00:34:48,420
Your clothes look really expensive too.

565
00:34:51,330 --> 00:34:53,900
- What body wash do you use? - What?

566
00:34:54,360 --> 00:34:56,630
My makeup is a sample Seon Mi gave me.

567
00:34:57,000 --> 00:34:58,900
And the neighbourhood chief gave me these clothes.

568
00:34:59,240 --> 00:35:00,300
I do not use body wash.

569
00:35:00,670 --> 00:35:01,700
Really?

570
00:35:02,540 --> 00:35:05,410
But the clothes look this good on you?

571
00:35:05,940 --> 00:35:08,410
Is it because you have a good figure?

572
00:35:08,480 --> 00:35:10,150
Is her shoulder your armrest?

573
00:35:10,610 --> 00:35:12,580
I took two days off filming for the commercial.

574
00:35:12,680 --> 00:35:13,950
Did you sort out the schedule?

575
00:35:14,680 --> 00:35:15,950
Well, not yet...

576
00:35:16,990 --> 00:35:18,960
You, go get me some water.

577
00:35:19,690 --> 00:35:20,690
Hurry.

578
00:35:25,160 --> 00:35:26,160
Hurry up.

579
00:35:29,630 --> 00:35:32,070
It is true. Those two have something going on.

580
00:35:32,640 --> 00:35:33,640
And they totally pretend they do not.

581
00:35:33,700 --> 00:35:35,440
- Um Tae Bong's acting is insane. - Right.

582
00:35:35,840 --> 00:35:37,440
No, looking at them again,

583
00:35:37,510 --> 00:35:38,940
it seems like they are not even that close.

584
00:35:39,340 --> 00:35:40,810
What? You said they seemed to be dating.

585
00:35:40,880 --> 00:35:43,210
No, they are not dating. I am absolutely sure.

586
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:45,380
- For real. - As if.

587
00:35:46,250 --> 00:35:47,280
What?

588
00:35:48,320 --> 00:35:50,120
The next national team gathering is at your restaurant again, right?

589
00:35:50,190 --> 00:35:51,420
Hey, let us change the venue for once...

590
00:35:51,720 --> 00:35:52,720
Anyway,

591
00:35:52,860 --> 00:35:54,390
about the Um Tae Bong case you asked me to look into.

592
00:35:54,490 --> 00:35:56,690
That parking lot is a blind spot for the security cameras,

593
00:35:57,230 --> 00:35:59,000
so this was caught on another car's dashcam.

594
00:36:03,670 --> 00:36:05,770
From now on, only come exactly three times a week.

595
00:36:05,840 --> 00:36:06,840
- What? - What?

596
00:36:09,010 --> 00:36:10,170
When did he leave?

597
00:36:11,510 --> 00:36:14,610
That customer is strange. He just left last time, too.

598
00:36:17,410 --> 00:36:19,380
I should have seen this face.

599
00:37:16,540 --> 00:37:18,410
Hong Du, I was just about to call you.

600
00:37:18,540 --> 00:37:21,040
- Today is the day we ride bicycles. - I am sorry.

601
00:37:21,110 --> 00:37:23,310
Um Tae Bong suddenly had a schedule earlier.

602
00:37:24,450 --> 00:37:25,720
It cannot be helped.

603
00:37:26,280 --> 00:37:28,850
- Work comes first. - Well,

604
00:37:28,920 --> 00:37:31,550
I could ditch it if you called me.

605
00:37:33,790 --> 00:37:35,220
I think you already ditched it.

606
00:37:40,260 --> 00:37:41,330
Here is something warm.

607
00:37:43,930 --> 00:37:46,270
Hong Du, I have been wanting to ask you this for a while...

608
00:37:46,340 --> 00:37:49,410
do you also like things like a doll keychain?

609
00:37:50,140 --> 00:37:51,240
Not really.

610
00:37:51,440 --> 00:37:53,540
Only a kid carries things like that around.

611
00:37:54,040 --> 00:37:55,240
What about when you were young?

612
00:37:55,710 --> 00:37:57,610
When you were about 8 or 9 years old?

613
00:37:58,310 --> 00:37:59,920
Like a car keychain...

614
00:38:03,350 --> 00:38:05,920
Never mind. Give it to me.

615
00:38:06,620 --> 00:38:08,660
If you were a girl, you would have liked...

616
00:38:08,720 --> 00:38:09,730
pretty dolls more.

617
00:38:11,260 --> 00:38:14,500
- That is a gender stereotype. - I am sorry.

618
00:38:14,900 --> 00:38:16,270
I went overboard with my kindness.

619
00:38:17,530 --> 00:38:20,640
I am generous, so I will understand. By the way,

620
00:38:20,700 --> 00:38:23,410
who carried around a car doll keychain?

621
00:38:24,670 --> 00:38:26,310
I am curious about that, too.

622
00:38:28,440 --> 00:38:29,580
There,

623
00:38:30,280 --> 00:38:33,450
it feels like there must have been...

624
00:38:34,920 --> 00:38:35,990
someone else there.

625
00:38:38,020 --> 00:38:39,090
There?

626
00:38:41,890 --> 00:38:45,160
Anyway, what do you like?

627
00:38:46,230 --> 00:38:47,230
Me?

628
00:38:48,360 --> 00:38:51,130
I just like people.

629
00:38:51,900 --> 00:38:52,900
Female people.

630
00:38:54,300 --> 00:38:55,340
What kind of female people?

631
00:38:57,570 --> 00:38:59,040
Don't tell me...

632
00:38:59,640 --> 00:39:01,110
Is it that woman you mentioned last time?

633
00:39:02,450 --> 00:39:04,410
I think you called her Oh Hae something.

634
00:39:04,480 --> 00:39:06,220
It is a misunderstanding. A total misunderstanding.

635
00:39:06,680 --> 00:39:08,120
It does not seem like a misunderstanding.

636
00:39:08,580 --> 00:39:10,290
Hong Du, when will you be free again?

637
00:39:11,050 --> 00:39:12,790
I told you I can skip work if you want me to, Mr. Han.

638
00:39:13,560 --> 00:39:14,590
- Can you really do that? - Yes.

639
00:39:15,890 --> 00:39:18,060
The bus is here. I will get going, Mr. Han.

640
00:39:18,530 --> 00:39:19,530
Okay.

641
00:39:36,210 --> 00:39:37,350
Hoped she'd take the next one.

642
00:39:40,850 --> 00:39:41,880
That startled me.

643
00:39:43,620 --> 00:39:45,050
She even shot a cosmetics commercial?

644
00:39:47,190 --> 00:39:48,720
She must be busy trying to become a building owner.

645
00:39:50,360 --> 00:39:51,890
Tae Bong, where is the commercial shoot tomorrow?

646
00:39:52,660 --> 00:39:56,400
No one will tell me. I will just send a coffee truck.

647
00:39:56,600 --> 00:39:57,670
I mean it.

648
00:39:57,730 --> 00:40:01,100
(Toxic Na Ri)

649
00:40:05,010 --> 00:40:06,040
I packed the toothpaste and toothbrush.

650
00:40:06,110 --> 00:40:07,580
Do I need to pack towels too? How many?

651
00:40:07,980 --> 00:40:09,110
Are you going on a school trip?

652
00:40:09,450 --> 00:40:10,610
This is my first time on a trip like this.

653
00:40:10,850 --> 00:40:12,550
We are going there to work.

654
00:40:12,820 --> 00:40:14,350
We shoot the commercial on the first day...

655
00:40:14,420 --> 00:40:15,850
and attend a party the next night.

656
00:40:16,790 --> 00:40:18,250
I am talking here.

657
00:40:19,990 --> 00:40:21,060
For 1 night and 2 days,

658
00:40:21,120 --> 00:40:22,120
do I need to pack two sets of clothes?

659
00:40:22,990 --> 00:40:23,990
What?

660
00:40:24,060 --> 00:40:25,830
Have you not been changing your clothes every day?

661
00:40:26,860 --> 00:40:28,430
Is there a time difference since it is out of town?

662
00:40:28,530 --> 00:40:29,530
How much?

663
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:31,600
There is no time difference.

664
00:40:33,940 --> 00:40:34,940
Unbelievable.

665
00:40:41,940 --> 00:40:43,010
Are you really going together?

666
00:40:45,580 --> 00:40:47,520
You have been acting a bit strange lately.

667
00:40:48,420 --> 00:40:49,950
It seems like you are treating her a lot better.

668
00:40:51,520 --> 00:40:52,590
Me?

669
00:40:52,890 --> 00:40:54,020
It is strange right now.

670
00:40:54,820 --> 00:40:56,790
It is not like you are taking care of a woman you like.

671
00:40:57,930 --> 00:40:58,930
Are you crazy?

672
00:40:59,760 --> 00:41:02,570
Out of all the actors, she specifically chose...

673
00:41:02,570 --> 00:41:04,930
me, so I figured there must be a reason.

674
00:41:05,270 --> 00:41:06,340
How should I put it?

675
00:41:07,470 --> 00:41:09,410
As someone who has captured women's hearts,

676
00:41:09,970 --> 00:41:11,270
it is a sense of responsibility, I guess?

677
00:41:14,210 --> 00:41:16,280
- Are you not going? - Yes, I am going.

678
00:41:16,710 --> 00:41:17,710
Hurry up and go.

679
00:41:21,280 --> 00:41:22,280
What is this?

680
00:41:24,790 --> 00:41:26,290
Did you pack everything in our house?

681
00:41:26,920 --> 00:41:28,990
I do not think I have packed everything yet.

682
00:41:30,430 --> 00:41:31,430
Are you that excited?

683
00:41:31,730 --> 00:41:33,060
Yes, I am going to sleep now.

684
00:41:33,130 --> 00:41:34,330
I need to sleep early so I can wake up early.

685
00:41:39,670 --> 00:41:41,070
My my.

686
00:42:11,970 --> 00:42:13,000
What a fuss.

687
00:42:22,110 --> 00:42:23,350
You must tell me every move the young lady makes...

688
00:42:23,410 --> 00:42:24,480
without leaving anything out.

689
00:42:29,350 --> 00:42:30,350
There.

690
00:42:37,760 --> 00:42:41,200
Our Tae Bong keeps asking about that person,

691
00:42:41,260 --> 00:42:42,560
so I do not know how to answer...

692
00:42:42,930 --> 00:42:46,200
Also, Tae Bong is going to a commercial shoot this time,

693
00:42:46,270 --> 00:42:47,400
and that person is going with him...

694
00:42:47,470 --> 00:42:48,500
Let's have a drink together.

695
00:42:51,770 --> 00:42:52,780
Yes, sir.

696
00:42:55,080 --> 00:42:56,080
Hello?

697
00:42:59,110 --> 00:43:01,750
I informed you that that person is going with him, yes.

698
00:43:02,420 --> 00:43:03,550
Done.

699
00:43:20,770 --> 00:43:22,170
I think we are short on outfits.

700
00:43:25,240 --> 00:43:26,740
It is Mr. Han.

701
00:43:28,040 --> 00:43:29,040
Do you know him?

702
00:43:29,910 --> 00:43:30,980
He lives next door to me.

703
00:43:32,510 --> 00:43:33,820
Why does he live next door to you?

704
00:43:34,650 --> 00:43:37,850
Jun Ji Hyun lives next door to me. Gang Dong Won lives two doors down,

705
00:43:37,920 --> 00:43:39,590
and Lee Min Ho lives three doors down.

706
00:43:44,360 --> 00:43:45,530
Is this the outfit for today?

707
00:43:46,200 --> 00:43:47,900
- Yes. - It is pretty.

708
00:43:52,200 --> 00:43:53,270
Hello.

709
00:43:55,270 --> 00:43:57,540
- You are here too, Hong Du. - Yes.

710
00:43:57,910 --> 00:44:00,210
- I am the head stylist. - I see.

711
00:44:00,710 --> 00:44:02,310
Let us go to the car to get more outfits.

712
00:44:06,220 --> 00:44:07,350
We will meet later.

713
00:44:11,890 --> 00:44:12,890
You saw the storyboard, right?

714
00:44:15,520 --> 00:44:17,890
It is so cliche.

715
00:44:18,090 --> 00:44:21,230
You were acting so confident,

716
00:44:21,300 --> 00:44:23,270
so I thought it would be an amazing concept.

717
00:44:23,330 --> 00:44:25,630
A commercial that makes you wonder if the client was on drugs,

718
00:44:26,200 --> 00:44:27,540
we want to make something like that too.

719
00:44:27,640 --> 00:44:29,910
But the actors say they do not want to do that.

720
00:44:30,810 --> 00:44:32,510
When we actually propose it, they say it looks cheap,

721
00:44:32,570 --> 00:44:34,510
it ruins their image, or it is cliche.

722
00:44:34,910 --> 00:44:38,050
Well-known actors can be quite picky.

723
00:44:43,520 --> 00:44:44,720
Are we not going to shoot?

724
00:44:47,460 --> 00:44:48,490
Keep up the good work, then.

725
00:44:48,960 --> 00:44:50,030
I will.

726
00:44:51,190 --> 00:44:52,190
Good luck.

727
00:44:53,860 --> 00:44:56,000
All right, this time,

728
00:44:56,070 --> 00:44:58,000
we will get a tight shot of your hand on the wheel,

729
00:44:58,830 --> 00:45:00,200
but the ring stands out too much.

730
00:45:03,210 --> 00:45:04,210
Ready for the shoot.

731
00:45:08,610 --> 00:45:10,280
He could just put it in his pocket for the shoot.

732
00:45:10,350 --> 00:45:11,580
Why did he leave it with me?

733
00:45:12,480 --> 00:45:13,720
Am I his storage box?

734
00:45:17,390 --> 00:45:18,790
Anyway, it is important to me.

735
00:45:18,920 --> 00:45:21,020
I was going to give it...

736
00:45:22,090 --> 00:45:23,160
to the first person I ever wanted.

737
00:45:27,630 --> 00:45:28,760
He is so petty.

738
00:45:30,670 --> 00:45:31,970
I will not wear it.

739
00:45:33,670 --> 00:45:34,670
Look at her slacking off.

740
00:45:34,740 --> 00:45:37,240
- Hey, Cha Hong Du, come here. - Yes.

741
00:45:45,410 --> 00:45:46,480
What is the room number?

742
00:45:48,480 --> 00:45:49,920
Great job on the shoot today, everyone.

743
00:45:50,320 --> 00:45:51,620
Get some good rest for today.

744
00:45:51,690 --> 00:45:53,920
I will see you tomorrow evening at the private party.

745
00:45:54,920 --> 00:45:56,260
The commercial team is having a team dinner...

746
00:45:56,330 --> 00:45:58,360
- on their way back to Seoul. - I know.

747
00:45:58,430 --> 00:45:59,430
It is a shame to just go to sleep.

748
00:45:59,500 --> 00:46:00,860
They say if you drink in a place with fresh air,

749
00:46:00,930 --> 00:46:02,330
you do not get a hangover.

750
00:46:04,030 --> 00:46:05,030
Hong Du,

751
00:46:05,230 --> 00:46:06,770
do you want to unpack and come down for a bit?

752
00:46:07,000 --> 00:46:09,200
There is a really nice place to take a walk around here.

753
00:46:09,710 --> 00:46:12,770
Really? Then give me 10 minutes. No, just 5 minutes.

754
00:46:13,540 --> 00:46:14,580
Great job, everyone.

755
00:46:14,940 --> 00:46:16,980
Dae-seong, please back up all the edited versions here.

756
00:46:18,110 --> 00:46:19,920
When I call you, run over within five seconds.

757
00:46:20,850 --> 00:46:23,520
- My working hours are over. - I will pay you overtime.

758
00:46:23,590 --> 00:46:25,590
Did you not see me make plans with Mr. Han earlier?

759
00:46:26,190 --> 00:46:29,790
Why do you keep calling him that? He is older than you.

760
00:46:30,330 --> 00:46:32,760
Close friends can do that. Why?

761
00:46:33,160 --> 00:46:34,160
Close?

762
00:46:35,500 --> 00:46:36,500
Double.

763
00:46:36,830 --> 00:46:39,670
- Triple. - No. Tonight is a night...

764
00:46:39,740 --> 00:46:42,440
where promises are more important than money.

765
00:46:43,010 --> 00:46:44,010
What night?

766
00:46:44,610 --> 00:46:46,240
What are you two going to do this late at night?

767
00:46:46,310 --> 00:46:48,510
Do you not feel the danger lurking all around you?

768
00:46:49,380 --> 00:46:50,410
You are unbelievable.

769
00:46:50,980 --> 00:46:52,010
Wow.

770
00:47:04,660 --> 00:47:05,730
Oh my.

771
00:47:06,460 --> 00:47:07,530
Do you work here?

772
00:47:08,230 --> 00:47:09,400
As you can see.

773
00:47:09,830 --> 00:47:11,300
That is great.

774
00:47:12,100 --> 00:47:14,370
I am attending the private party,

775
00:47:15,070 --> 00:47:16,470
and there is a VIP room, right?

776
00:47:17,510 --> 00:47:20,410
Unfortunately, this event is only for customers...

777
00:47:20,480 --> 00:47:21,980
who purchased the limited edition new car.

778
00:47:22,280 --> 00:47:25,550
What? Limited? How much is it? I will buy it.

779
00:47:25,910 --> 00:47:27,080
Call the manager.

780
00:47:27,680 --> 00:47:28,720
Director Han,

781
00:47:29,350 --> 00:47:30,890
I have finished guiding everyone to their rooms.

782
00:47:34,120 --> 00:47:35,720
So you are the manager?

783
00:47:36,020 --> 00:47:37,330
As you can see.

784
00:47:38,630 --> 00:47:41,260
Um Tae Bong's real girlfriend, Song Na Ri.

785
00:47:42,400 --> 00:47:44,270
Probably the one Um Tae Bong sang for that day.

786
00:47:44,670 --> 00:47:45,670
Yes.

787
00:47:46,600 --> 00:47:47,970
Where is Director Han?

788
00:47:51,470 --> 00:47:54,440
Here you are. The view is terrible.

789
00:47:54,780 --> 00:47:56,450
Whether you are Mr. Han or Director Han,

790
00:47:56,510 --> 00:47:58,780
do not go anywhere and change my room...

791
00:47:59,310 --> 00:48:00,550
Tae Bong.

792
00:48:01,180 --> 00:48:02,180
You...

793
00:48:14,660 --> 00:48:16,530
Now, focus.

794
00:48:18,170 --> 00:48:20,600
To celebrate Song Na Ri's birthday that is coming up in four months.

795
00:48:21,200 --> 00:48:23,210
- Cheers. - Cheers.

796
00:48:23,270 --> 00:48:24,410
- Cheers. - Thank you.

797
00:48:24,470 --> 00:48:26,840
- Happy birthday. - Happy birthday, Song Na Ri.

798
00:48:26,940 --> 00:48:28,910
You are the best, Tae Bong.

799
00:48:32,210 --> 00:48:34,520
Hey. Do you want to die?

800
00:48:34,750 --> 00:48:35,750
Drink.

801
00:48:41,590 --> 00:48:43,330
I am finally drinking.

802
00:48:46,090 --> 00:48:48,360
You should not be drinking. You are Tae Bong's bodyguard.

803
00:48:48,930 --> 00:48:49,930
What?

804
00:48:53,670 --> 00:48:55,470
You knew?

805
00:48:55,770 --> 00:48:57,740
Wow, do you think I am an idiot?

806
00:48:58,240 --> 00:48:59,440
I knew it when you fought...

807
00:48:59,510 --> 00:49:01,340
that weird fan who grabbed my waist.

808
00:49:04,450 --> 00:49:05,910
What?

809
00:49:06,480 --> 00:49:08,820
Did everyone know?

810
00:49:09,480 --> 00:49:10,790
